# C reference model (cmodel) build tree — regenerated by `make`
software/cmodel/build/

# ── Generated weight blob ────────────────────────────
#  software/export/weights.hex is a byte-for-byte concatenation of the
#  per-layer *_w.hex files that are already tracked, in program order. 8.8 MB
#  of pure duplication, and one command rebuilds it:
#      python scripts/gen_program.py --emit
#  The small params_*.hex are tracked, because they are NOT a concatenation:
#  they materialise the RES_ADD and GAP constants per channel.
software/export/weights.hex

# ── Synthesis artifacts ──────────────────────────────
#  The .rpt files are small and are the evidence behind the numbers in
#  docs/, so they stay. The checkpoint and the tool log are large and
#  regenerable with: bash scripts/run_synth.sh
build/synth/*.dcp
build/synth/vivado.log
build/synth/*.jou
#  The timing reports are ~1 MB of text between them. utilization.rpt and
#  utilization_hier.rpt are small and stay; DD-018 quotes the timing numbers
#  that matter (WNS, the logic/route split, the 27-deep DSP cascade) verbatim.
build/synth/timing_paths.rpt
build/synth/timing_summary.rpt
.Xil/
build/synth/*backup.log
#  scripts/synth.tcl takes TOP now, and a non-default top writes to
#  build/synth_<top>/ so accel_top and accel_sys can be compared without one
#  overwriting the other. Same rule for those: the two utilization reports stay
#  as the evidence, everything else is regenerable with
#      TOP=accel_sys bash scripts/run_synth.sh
build/synth_*/*.dcp
build/synth_*/vivado.log
build/synth_*/*.jou
build/synth_*/*backup.log
build/synth_*/timing_paths.rpt
build/synth_*/timing_summary.rpt

# ── Place-and-route artifacts (scripts/run_impl.sh) ──
#  Same rule as build/synth above, one directory per constraint so two runs can
#  be compared. The utilization reports are small and are the evidence behind
#  the before/after tables in docs/, so they stay. Checkpoints, tool logs and
#  the ~3 MB timing reports are regenerable with:
#      PERIOD=4.000 bash scripts/run_impl.sh
#  and the numbers that matter (WNS, TNS, the worst path, the logic/route split)
#  are quoted verbatim in docs/lab_notebook.md.
build/impl_*/*.dcp
build/impl_*/vivado.log
build/impl_*/*.jou
build/impl_*/*backup.log
build/impl_*/timing_paths.rpt
build/impl_*/timing_summary.rpt
build/impl_*/synth_timing_summary.rpt
#  The methodology report is ~6 MB; the DPIR-2 count that matters is on stdout
#  and quoted in docs/.
build/impl_*/methodology.rpt
#  The period-overridden XDC is a generated copy of the committed one. The
#  pattern is per-top now, because impl.tcl takes TOP and writes
#  ${top}_ooc_${period}.xdc - naming only accel_top here left the accel_sys and
#  accel_axi copies tracked, which is a generated file in the repository.
build/impl_*/*_ooc_*.xdc

# ── Vivado GUI project ───────────────────────────────
#  Entirely regenerable, and it references sources where they live, so nothing
#  here is a source of truth. Delete it and re-run whenever:
#      vivado -mode batch -source scripts/make_project.tcl
build/vivado/

# ── Golden vector sets ───────────────────────────────
#  Each set is 28 MB of hex: one file per layer for one image. They are
#  DERIVED - `export.py --image <path>` regenerates any of them exactly, given
#  the checkpoint (which is in LFS above, for precisely this reason).
#
#  So exactly one set is tracked: the one hardware/tb points at. The others are
#  local artifacts. To reproduce the per-class verification table in
#  docs/lab_notebook.md:
#
#      cd software/train && python export.py --data ../../data/grape \
#          --ckpt ../runs/mobilenetv2_grape.pth --scales quant_scales.json \
#          --image <image> --check 0
#      python scripts/gen_program.py --emit --golden-dir software/golden/<set>
#      bash scripts/run_sim.sh accel accel_top ...
software/golden/*/
!software/golden/healthy_hl6025/
#  image_1 is 2026-06 and cannot be regenerated: its source image is gone from
#  data/ and its checkpoint was overwritten. Its blobs are already in history,
#  so excluding it here would save nothing; kept, marked stale in its manifest.
!software/golden/image_1/

# ── Claude project context ───────────────────────────
#  Working notes kept for an assistant's context, not part of the thesis or the
#  build: nothing in the repo reads them and nothing regenerates them. Local
#  only, by decision 2026-09-25.
docs/claude_project/
